From 31dc9ac16245c2eed69d29b80da6efa38d7f30a2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tianyu9748 <54686548+Tianyu9748@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 16:13:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03/26] [Diffusion] ReelCache server flags and
 causal_kv_session request handle

- ServerArgs.reelcache_config (ReelCacheArgs): --reelcache-enable, --reelcache-config
  (JSON object or file), --reelcache-hevc-inter-prediction (BooleanOptional,
  default off). Enabled servers check at startup that
  reelcache.integrations.sglang is importable and fail explicitly otherwise;
  ReelCache cannot be combined with --kv-cache-quant and is single-GPU for now.
- The GPU worker attaches the backend after building the pipeline
  (attach_causal_kv_backend); disabled workers import nothing from ReelCache.
- SamplingParams.causal_kv_session (+ --causal-kv-session): validated
  plain-data handle {session_id, action generate|resume|fork|rewind,
  pause_after_chunks, from_session, checkpoint, replace}; part of the batch
  signature so requests of different sessions are never merged.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
